Case 08 — Method D (6x6 Mini Sudoku build) — solar-open2 vs solar-pro4
Date: 2026-08-04 (local, sequential, shared Tier-0 UPSTAGE_API_KEY)
Harness: omp (oh-my-pi), `omp --print --auto-approve --max-time 8m`
Prompt: 08-omp-solar-open2/scripts/sudoku-prompt.txt (identical for both)
Gate:   08-omp-solar-open2/scripts/verify-sudoku.mjs (Playwright, 6 checks)

WHY THIS RUN EXISTS
-------------------
An audit of this repo's 2026-08-03 local verification logs found Method D
had been SKIPPED (SKIP_METHOD_D=1) for both models, so no sudoku was
actually built in that round, and the single published gallery entry
carried no model attribution. This run builds it for real, per model.

RAW SINGLE-SHOT RESULT (before any fix round)
---------------------------------------------
Both models produced an index.html on the first attempt. Neither passed
the spec gate unedited:

  solar-open2  -> renders, but initPuzzle() assigns `givenCells = removed`
                  and then renders `input.value = puzzle[row][col]` for
                  cells IN that set. `removed` is the set of cells the
                  generator BLANKED (set to 0), so the logic is inverted:
                  blank cells render as the literal "0" and the real
                  givens render empty.
                  Gate: ✗ "given cell cell-0-2 has invalid value 0"

  solar-pro4   -> hard JavaScript syntax error, line 245:
                    var positions = shuffle positions = shufflePositions();
                  Throws "Unexpected identifier 'positions'", so the whole
                  script dies and the board never renders.
                  Gate: ✗ "expected 36 cell inputs, found 0"

ASK-VERIFY-FIX LOOP (same methodology the existing gallery entry used —
the model is asked to fix its own bug; no hand-written code substituted)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  solar-pro4   -> 1 round. Given the exact malformed line, it replaced it
                  with `var positions = shufflePositions();` and changed
                  nothing else.
                  Gate after fix: ✓ 6/6 ALL PASS.

  solar-open2  -> 3 rounds attempted, still failing at cutoff:
                  round 1 (inversion, verbose prompt) — Deadline exceeded
                          at the 8m cap, no edit written.
                  round 2 (inversion, tightened single-line prompt) —
                          succeeded; rewrote the assignment to build
                          givenCells as the complement of `removed`.
                          Gate then surfaced a DEEPER pre-existing bug:
                          ✗ "given cells conflict at cell-5-1 (puzzle
                          generation is broken)".
                          Root cause (read by hand): generateFullGrid()
                          pre-fills fillBox(0,0), fillBox(2,0), fillBox(4,0)
                          under the comment "Fill diagonal boxes first
                          (they don't affect each other)" — but in a 6x6
                          grid with 2-row x 3-col boxes those three boxes
                          all occupy columns 0-2, so they very much do
                          conflict. The comment's premise is simply wrong.
                  round 3 (targeted at that generation bug) — Deadline
                          exceeded at 8m again, no edit written.

HEAD-TO-HEAD SUMMARY
--------------------
| | solar-open2 | solar-pro4 |
| Produced an index.html first try | yes | yes |
| Passed the gate unedited | no | no |
| Failure class | logic (inverted set) + invalid grid generation | syntax error |
| Fix rounds to green | not reached (3 attempted, 2 timed out at 8m) | 1 |
| Final gate | ✗ (this run) | ✓ 6/6 |

On this task, in this run, solar-pro4 was decisively better: its single
defect was mechanical and it repaired it in one pass, while solar-open2
had two stacked logic defects and twice exhausted the 8-minute agentic
budget without emitting an edit. One run each is not a benchmark — but
it is a real, reproducible difference on a real task, not a smoke test.

